{"id":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#lem:asymptotic-ray","title":"lem:asymptotic-ray","path":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature.md","line":333,"body":"","kind":"lemma","status":"not_started","tex":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature.tex#lem:asymptotic-ray","uses":["[[references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#def:busemann-function]]","[[references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#def:asymptotic-ray]]","[[references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#lem:busemann-approx-antitone]]","[[references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#lem:busemann-limit]]","[[references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#lem:busemann-lipschitz]]","[[references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#lem:busemann-le-approx]]","[[references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#lem:busemann-along-ray]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature.tex","label":"lem:asymptotic-ray","line":573,"source":"\\begin{lemma}[Busemann values along asymptotic rays]\n\\label{lem:asymptotic-ray}\n\n\\uses{def:busemann-function, def:asymptotic-ray}\n\n\n\n\nIf $\\mu$ is asymptotic to $\\lambda$ and $x=\\mu(0)$, then\n$$B_\\lambda(\\mu(s))=B_\\lambda(x)-s\\qquad(s\\ge0).$$\n\\end{lemma}\n\\begin{proof}\n\\sketch\n\n\\uses{lem:busemann-approx-antitone,lem:busemann-limit,lem:busemann-lipschitz,lem:busemann-le-approx,lem:busemann-along-ray}\nFor witnessing segments $\\sigma_n$ from $x$ to $\\lambda(t_n)$,\nminimality gives\n$$B_{\\lambda,t_n}(\\sigma_n(s))=B_{\\lambda,t_n}(x)-s.$$\nUse local uniform convergence, monotonicity of the approximants, and\ntheir convergence at $x$ to obtain\n$B_\\lambda(\\mu(s))\\le B_\\lambda(x)-s$. The reverse inequality follows\nfrom the $1$-Lipschitz property and $d(x,\\mu(s))=s$.\n\\end{proof}","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Lemma</div></section>[Busemann values along asymptotic rays] <span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-6c656d3a6173796d70746f7469632d726179\"></span> <p></p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FMorganTian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature%23def%3Abusemann-function\">↗ def:busemann-function</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FMorganTian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature%23def%3Aasymptotic-ray\">↗ def:asymptotic-ray</a> <p></p>If <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\mu $\">$\\mu $</span> is asymptotic to <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\lambda $\">$\\lambda $</span> and <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$x=\\mu (0)$\">$x=\\mu (0)$</span>, then <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"true\" data-tex=\"\\[ B_\\lambda (\\mu (s))=B_\\lambda (x)-s\\qquad (s\\ge 0). \\]\">\\[ B_\\lambda (\\mu (s))=B_\\lambda (x)-s\\qquad (s\\ge 0). \\]</span>  <section class=\"theorem proof\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Proof</div><p>\\sketch </p><p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FMorganTian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature%23lem%3Abusemann-approx-antitone\">↗ lem:busemann-approx-antitone</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FMorganTian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature%23lem%3Abusemann-limit\">↗ lem:busemann-limit</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FMorganTian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature%23lem%3Abusemann-lipschitz\">↗ lem:busemann-lipschitz</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FMorganTian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature%23lem%3Abusemann-le-approx\">↗ lem:busemann-le-approx</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FMorganTian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature%23lem%3Abusemann-along-ray\">↗ lem:busemann-along-ray</a> For witnessing segments <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\sigma _n$\">$\\sigma _n$</span> from <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$x$\">$x$</span> to <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\lambda (t_n)$\">$\\lambda (t_n)$</span>, minimality gives </p><p><span class=\"math\" data-display=\"true\" data-tex=\"\\[ B_{\\lambda ,t_n}(\\sigma _n(s))=B_{\\lambda ,t_n}(x)-s. \\]\">\\[ B_{\\lambda ,t_n}(\\sigma _n(s))=B_{\\lambda ,t_n}(x)-s. \\]</span></p><p> Use local uniform convergence, monotonicity of the approximants, and their convergence at <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$x$\">$x$</span> to obtain <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$B_\\lambda (\\mu (s))\\le B_\\lambda (x)-s$\">$B_\\lambda (\\mu (s))\\le B_\\lambda (x)-s$</span>. The reverse inequality follows from the <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$1$\">$1$</span>-Lipschitz property and <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$d(x,\\mu (s))=s$\">$d(x,\\mu (s))=s$</span>. </p><span class=\"qed\" aria-label=\"证毕\" style=\"display:block;text-align:right\">□</span></section>","warnings":["部分 TeX 排版细节未完整还原（已保留可读内容）: sketch"]},"previous":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#lem:asymptotic-ray-exists","next":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#cor:asymptotic-ray-busemann-bound","relations":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#def:busemann-function","title":"def:busemann-function","label":"def:busemann-function"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#def:asymptotic-ray","title":"def:asymptotic-ray","label":"def:asymptotic-ray"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#lem:busemann-approx-antitone","title":"lem:busemann-approx-antitone","label":"lem:busemann-approx-antitone"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#lem:busemann-limit","title":"lem:busemann-limit","label":"lem:busemann-limit"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#lem:busemann-lipschitz","title":"lem:busemann-lipschitz","label":"lem:busemann-lipschitz"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#lem:busemann-le-approx","title":"lem:busemann-le-approx","label":"lem:busemann-le-approx"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#lem:busemann-along-ray","title":"lem:busemann-along-ray","label":"lem:busemann-along-ray"}],"backlinks":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#cor:asymptotic-ray-busemann-bound","title":"cor:asymptotic-ray-busemann-bound","label":"cor:asymptotic-ray-busemann-bound"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#lem:busemann-gradient-norm-one","title":"lem:busemann-gradient-norm-one","label":"lem:busemann-gradient-norm-one"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#line","title":"line","label":"line"}],"copy_context":{"version":1,"level":0,"node":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#lem:asymptotic-ray","title":"lem:asymptotic-ray","tex":"\\begin{lemma}[Busemann values along asymptotic rays]\n\\label{lem:asymptotic-ray}\n\n\\uses{def:busemann-function, def:asymptotic-ray}\n\n\n\n\nIf $\\mu$ is asymptotic to $\\lambda$ and $x=\\mu(0)$, then\n$$B_\\lambda(\\mu(s))=B_\\lambda(x)-s\\qquad(s\\ge0).$$\n\\end{lemma}\n\\begin{proof}\n\\sketch\n\n\\uses{lem:busemann-approx-antitone,lem:busemann-limit,lem:busemann-lipschitz,lem:busemann-le-approx,lem:busemann-along-ray}\nFor witnessing segments $\\sigma_n$ from $x$ to $\\lambda(t_n)$,\nminimality gives\n$$B_{\\lambda,t_n}(\\sigma_n(s))=B_{\\lambda,t_n}(x)-s.$$\nUse local uniform convergence, monotonicity of the approximants, and\ntheir convergence at $x$ to obtain\n$B_\\lambda(\\mu(s))\\le B_\\lambda(x)-s$. The reverse inequality follows\nfrom the $1$-Lipschitz property and $d(x,\\mu(s))=s$.\n\\end{proof}","source":"tex/references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature.tex","description":"","dependencies":[{"node":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#def:busemann-function","title":"def:busemann-function","description":""},{"node":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#def:asymptotic-ray","title":"def:asymptotic-ray","description":""},{"node":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#lem:busemann-approx-antitone","title":"lem:busemann-approx-antitone","description":""},{"node":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#lem:busemann-limit","title":"lem:busemann-limit","description":""},{"node":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#lem:busemann-lipschitz","title":"lem:busemann-lipschitz","description":""},{"node":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#lem:busemann-le-approx","title":"lem:busemann-le-approx","description":""},{"node":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#lem:busemann-along-ray","title":"lem:busemann-along-ray","description":""}],"dependencies_omitted":0,"unresolved_dependencies":[],"unresolved_omitted":0}}